Dear Ede,
\f1 \

\f0 \
This is Margarida with Open Ephys. Thanks for reaching out.
\f1 \

\f0 \
The Harp Load Cells Interface controls up to 2 load cells readers, digital outputs can be regulated at 3V or 5V.
\f1 \
\

\f0 Please note that the Harp Load Cells Interface has to be connected to the Harp Load Cells Reader.\'a0The Harp Load Cells Reader is compatible with 4-wire load cells sensors with 5V power supply and with an input signal range maximum of 4mV. Each\'a0Harp Load Cells Reader controls up to 4 load cell sensors, at 1kHz sampling rate.
\f1 \
\

\f0 You can find more information about the Harp Load Cells device\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cf-hw.org/open-source-tools/electronic-devices/load-cells"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 here}}. Additionally, you can read about its features, connectivity and interface in the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/harp-tech/device.loadcells"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 GitHub repository}}\'a0and reach out to the\'a0developers by posting in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/orgs/harp-tech/discussions"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 Harp project GitHub discussions}}.
\f1 \

\f0 \
The Harp Load Cells devices, as well as other Harp devices, are currently being widely used at the Allen Institute.
\f1 \

\f0 \
I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.
\f1 \

\f0 \
Best wishes,\uc0\u8232 Margarida Baeta
